Apple's new iPhone lineup asks buyers a new and challenging question: Is a foldable display worth feature compromises?<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/iPhone-Duo-vs-18-Pro-Buyers-Guide-Feature.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1065541" /><br/>
Alongside the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-18-pro/">iPhone 18 Pro</a> and &zwnj;iPhone 18 Pro&zwnj; Max, which start at &#36;1,199 and &#36;1,299 respectively, there is now the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a>, Apple's first foldable iPhone, which starts at &#36;1,999. All three are brand new, all three feature the same A20 Pro chip, and all three sit at the top end of Apple's lineup.<br/>
<br/>
The Duo is not a Pro model, though, and Apple's own wording makes that clear. For example, its rear camera array is branded the 48-megapixel Dual Fusion system rather than the Pro Fusion system, and the word Pro appears nowhere in its name. The &#36;700 premium over the &zwnj;iPhone 18 Pro&zwnj; Max buys a folding 7.6-inch display, not a better camera.<br/>
<br/>
All three models still share a large amount of hardware. The shared features include:<br/>
<br/>
<ul><br/>
<li>A20 Pro chip with a 6-core CPU, 7-core GPU with Neural Accelerators, dual 16-core Neural Engine, and hardware-accelerated ray tracing</li><br/>
<li>Apple C2 modem (except on the Pro Max in the United States), N1 wireless networking chip, Wi-Fi 7, Bluetooth 6, Thread, and the second-generation Ultra Wideband chip</li><br/>
<li>Super Retina XDR <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/macbook-ultra/">OLED</a> displays with ProMotion up to 120Hz, Always-On display, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/dynamic-island/">Dynamic Island</a>, and 3000 nits of peak outdoor brightness</li><br/>
<li>Ceramic Shield 2 front with 3x better scratch resistance, Ceramic Shield back, and IP68 water resistance to a depth of 6 meters</li><br/>
<li>Camera Control, a 48MP Fusion Ultra Wide camera at 13mm and f/2.2, Photographic Styles 3, Dual Capture, smart focus tracking, and 48MP macro photography</li><br/>
<li><a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-intelligence/">Apple Intelligence</a> and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a> AI in <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a></li><br/>
<li>Emergency SOS, Crash Detection, Roadside Assistance, Messages, and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/find-my/">Find My</a> via satellite</li><br/>
